<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claros</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Claros was an ancient sanctuary and oracle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, in the territory of Colophon near modern Ahmetbeyli in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Its oracle, delivered through a priest who drank from a sacred spring, was among the most famous of the Greek world and flourished especially in the Roman imperial period. The temple ruins were excavated in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claros.jpg" alt="Claros" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikater · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klaros01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
